## Meta Key Naming Convention
Canonical reference: `mu-brighter-support-main/Naming-conventions.md` — Database & Storage section.
When this rule and that doc conflict, the doc wins. Update both together.

### Prefixes

| Prefix | Scope | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| `scos_seo_` | SEO module meta | `scos_seo_focus_keyword` |
| `scos_ca_` | Content Architecture module meta | `scos_topic` |
| `scos_sa_` | Social Amplification module meta | `scos_sa_generated_caption` |
| `scos_cpt_` | Post Type / CPT customisation meta | `scos_cpt_icon` |
| `se_` | Site-wide settings not owned by any single module | `se_ga4_id`, `se_site_launched_at` |

### Options Prefixes

| Prefix | Scope | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| `site_essentials_` | Plugin-level config — activation, version, internal flags | `site_essentials_version` |
| `se_` | Site-wide user-configurable settings | `se_ga4_id`, `se_agency_name`, `se_support_manual_full` |
| `scos_` | SCOS module-level settings stored as options | `scos_sa_default_tone` |

### Rules

- ALL new meta and option keys MUST follow the prefix conventions above
- `scos_[module]_` owns module-specific meta — even if another module reads it
- `se_` is for settings genuinely global or shared across two or more modules — when in doubt, use `se_`
- If a setting starts in one module but will clearly be used globally (e.g. API keys), use `se_` from the start
- NEVER create new keys with `bw_` prefix — deprecated, pending migration
- If you encounter `bw_` keys in existing code, flag with `// TODO: migrate to scos_ or se_` but do NOT auto-rename
- _seopress_ is read-only legacy migration fallback, do not write to it in new code
- Legacy inconsistencies exist throughout the codebase — flag them, never silently "fix" them

### Format

- Always lowercase, words separated by underscores
- Post meta: `scos_[module]_[fieldname]` or `se_[fieldname]`
- Options: `site_essentials_[name]` / `se_[name]` / `scos_[module]_[name]`
- Transients: `se_[name]`
- ACF field keys: `field_scos_[module]_[fieldname]`

### Why this matters

Clean prefix patterns enable precise WP-CLI and MCP scoped queries:
`wp post meta list --keys=scos_sa_%` scopes exactly to Social Amplification.
Treat naming as infrastructure. It enables safe bulk operations, safe DB cleanup,
and unambiguous Claude CLI/MCP tool queries without manual scoping every time.

